<title>RUSSIA: Russian 6-mth t-bill yield rises to 82.62 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 6-mth t-bill yield rises to 82.62 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month GKO discount Treasury bills rose sharply to 82.62 percent at an auction on Wednesday from 61.25 percent at the previous auction on September 18, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast an average yield in the 75-85 percent range.</p>
<p>				     Sept 25	     Sept 18</p>
<p>    Series number		22051		 22050</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 7.00 trln rbls    7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million	    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	     6.81 trln	   7.93 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	     6.32 trln	   6.78 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		     4.11 trln	   4.93 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	     64.99 pct	   72.68 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price   62.00 pct	   71.73 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     82.62 pct	   61.25 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield  94.00 pct	   64.22 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			  238 days	    224 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		   Sept 25	     Sept 18</p>
<p>    Maturity date		May 21, 1997	April 30, 1997</p>
<p>Earlier the finance ministry raised 3.19 trillion roubles when it auctioned a new four trillion rouble issue of three-month T-bills, 1997, taking total proceeds from today's auctions to about 7.3 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>The finance ministry also repaid about seven trillion roubles in a maturing issue of six-month T-bills.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
